            <ArticleTitle>Granulomatous hepatitis induced by aspirin-kodein analgesics.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>279-81</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Salicylate-kodein is a widely used analgesic agent, particularly in outpatient practice. Salicylates have been incriminated in hepatic injury while kodein may induce biliary spasm. We report here a case of granulomatous hepatitis attributed to prolonged intake of this combination, which has never been reported previously to our knowledge.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
